{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"two-religion","type":"text","text":"## Two-Religion Model\n\n**4 evidence types · 10 HIGH+ supports · 0 contradicts**\nElite vs. folk — the graph's operating framework.\n\n**Evidence:** archaeology (figurines, shrines, cult\nstands), iconography (Keel/Uehlinger motif analysis),\nbiblical text (prophetic polemics), sociology\n(regional vs. centralized worship)\n\n**Scholars:** Dever · Keel & Uehlinger · Sommer · Albertz · Zevit\n\n**Challenge:** None at MEDIUM+. Archaeological +\ntextual convergence makes this structurally robust.\n\nKaufmann dissent: NO","x":-85,"y":-1000,"width":400,"height":480,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"kenite-midianite","type":"text","text":"## Kenite/Midianite Hypothesis\n\n**Plausible · unproven · LOW-MEDIUM confidence**\nHow Yahweh moved from south to Israel.\n\n**Evidence:** Exod 18 (Jethro), Num 10 (Hobab),\nSoleb \"Shasu of Yhw,\" Midianite pottery\n\n**Scholars:** Romer (\"best available explanation\")\n\n**Challenge:** Moses has no extrabiblical attestation.\nFleming: Yahweh not taken from outsiders — name\nreflects Israel's own diverse origins. Cannot be\nverified archaeologically.\n\nKaufmann dissent: NO","x":-190,"y":-1930,"width":380,"height":490,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"el-priority","type":"text","text":"## El's Priority\n\n**4 evidence types · 16 HIGH+ supports · 0 contradicts**\nGraph's strongest single convergence.\n\n**Evidence:** onomastics (\"Israel\" = \"El strives\"),\nbiblical text (Deut 32:8-9, Exod 6:2-3),\narchaeology (El sanctuaries), comparative ANE\n(Ugaritic El council)\n\n**Scholars:** Smith · Day · Romer · Lewis · Cross · Keel\n\n**Challenge:** Kaufmann dissents (37+ contradict\nedges) but is isolated. Not falsified — structural tension.\n\n⚠️ Kaufmann dissent: YES","x":-1760,"y":-1080,"width":400,"height":480,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"divine-council","type":"text","text":"## Divine Council Interpretation\n\n**Text not disputed · interpretation is the debate**\nYahweh presides over subordinate divine beings.\n\n**Evidence:** Ps 82, Deut 32:8-9, 1 Kgs 22, Job 1-2;\nUgaritic parallels (El's council, four-tier pantheon)\n\n**Polytheistic survivals:** Smith (HIGH)\n**Created divine beings:** Heiser (MED, 1 support)\n**Fluid manifestations:** Sommer (HIGH)\n\n**Challenge:** Same texts, three frameworks. Heiser's\ninstitutional isolation outside critical citation\nnetwork — position may be stronger than graph shows.\n\nKaufmann dissent: NO","x":1760,"y":1440,"width":400,"height":480,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"el-clan-deity","type":"text","text":"## El: Family/Clan Deity\n\n**6 HIGH+ supports · 0 contradicts**\nDifferent profile from national warrior Yahweh.\n\n**Evidence:** patriarchal El epithets (El Shaddai, El\nElyon, etc.), Gen 49:25 (fertility domain) vs. Exod\n15:3 (martial domain), Ugaritic El as aged patriarch\n\n**Scholars:** Lewis · Day · Keel · Cross\n\n**Challenge:** None at MEDIUM+. Converges with\nEl's Priority. Two-stage development: clan-based El\nreligion overlaid by national Yahweh cult.\n\nKaufmann dissent: NO","x":-650,"y":1290,"width":380,"height":470,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"canaanite-transform","type":"text","text":"## Canaanite Myth Transformed\n\n**8 HIGH+ supports · 0 contradicts**\nMonotheism repurposed inherited mythology.\n\n**Evidence:** Ps 74 (Leviathan = Baal's Litanu), Ps 29\n(Baal hymn reattributed), Exod 15 (Song of the Sea\nmirrors Baal's defeat of Yamm), Ugaritic Baal Cycle\n\n**Scholars:** Smith · Day · Cross · Romer\n\n**Challenge:** None at MEDIUM+. Convergence-and-\ndifferentiation framework is consensus. Kaufmann\ndissents on comparative method but is isolated.\n\nKaufmann dissent: NO","x":960,"y":640,"width":400,"height":440,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"archaeology-primary","type":"text","text":"## Archaeology as Primary Source\n\n**9 HIGH+ supports · 0 contradicts**\nTexts = elite theology; material culture = practiced religion.\n\n**Evidence:** 3000+ JPFs in domestic contexts, cult\nstands (Taanach), domestic shrines (Tell Beit\nMirsim), mortuary evidence, Dever's 8 categories\nof archaeological evidence for folk religion\n\n**Scholars:** Dever · Keel & Uehlinger · Zevit · Stavrakopoulou\n\n**Challenge:** None at MEDIUM+. Methodological\nprinciple widely accepted. Indirect tension with\nKaufmann's textual primacy.\n\nKaufmann dissent: NO","x":1070,"y":-1000,"width":400,"height":480,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"southern-origin","type":"text","text":"## Southern Origin\n\n**4 evidence types · 6+ scholars HIGH+ · 0 contradicts**\nYahweh came from Edom/Midian/Seir/Teman.\n\n**Evidence:** Egyptian epigraphy (Soleb \"Shasu of\nYhw\"), biblical poetry (Deut 33:2, Judg 5:4-5,\nHab 3:3, Ps 68), onomastics, archaeology\n(Midianite pottery)\n\n**Scholars:** Smith · Day · Romer · Lewis · Cross · Keel\n\n**Challenge:** Fleming — Seir may not be in original\nSoleb list (column-space calc). Yhwʒ as people-name,\nnot divine name. Not yet rebutted in graph.\n\nKaufmann dissent: NO","x":-880,"y":-1240,"width":400,"height":480,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"jerusalem-centralization","type":"text","text":"## Jerusalem Centralization\n\n**7 HIGH+ supports · 0 contradicts**\nJosiah's late 7th c. political project.\n\n**Evidence:** 2 Kgs 22-23 (\"book of the law\"\nfound), Deut 12 (single sanctuary command),\nArad temple decommissioned late 7th c., regional\nshrines abandoned same period\n\n**Scholars:** Romer · Smith · Albertz · Dever · Sommer\n\n**Challenge:** Kaufmann dissents — argues\ncentralization was Mosaic and original. Isolated\n(1 MEDIUM+ contradiction on candidate list).\n\n⚠️ Kaufmann dissent: YES","x":3200,"y":-1120,"width":400,"height":460,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"zoroastrian","type":"text","text":"## Zoroastrian Influence\n\n**Parallels exist · dating uncertain · LOW confidence**\nDirection of influence debated.\n\n**Evidence:** comparative religion (dualism,\nresurrection, angelology/demonology)\n\n**Scholars:** Smith: \"reinforced but not progenitor\"\n\n**Challenge:** Avesta dating notoriously difficult.\nIsraelite monotheistic trajectory predates Persian\ncontact. Direction may be Israel → Persia, not reverse.\n\nKaufmann dissent: NO","x":3225,"y":-2210,"width":350,"height":490,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"monotheism-timing","type":"text","text":"## Monotheism Timing\n\n**Strong mechanism · two anomalies · not fully settled**\nExilic crisis vs. early revolution.\n\n**Evidence:** biblical text (Second Isaiah — first\nunambiguous denial of other gods), historical\nreconstruction (exile as catalyst), onomastics\n(Tigay: 94%+ Yahwistic names), Elephantine\npapyri (Anat-Yahu in 5th c.)\n\n**Late:** Romer · Smith · Dever · Day · Albertz\n**Early:** Kaufmann (MED-HIGH, 0 support edges)\n**Challenge:** Tigay (onomastic data)\n\n**Challenge:** Elephantine anomaly (polytheism after\nexile). Tigay's names suggest early monolatry.\nKaufmann isolated but not falsified.\n\n⚠️ Kaufmann dissent: YES","x":2160,"y":-1975,"width":400,"height":510,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"what-happened-goddess","type":"text","text":"## What Happened to the Goddess\n\n**Speculative · 3 scholars at MEDIUM**\nFemale divine imagery absorbed, not eliminated.\n\n**Evidence:** Prov 8 (Woman Wisdom), Ezek 16\n(personified Jerusalem), Isa 66 (Zion as mother);\ngoddess → abstraction pattern\n\n**Scholars:** Smith · Day · Romer (all MEDIUM)\n\n**Challenge:** Absorption model suggestive but not\nconclusive. \"Replacement consorts\" — Smith's own\nframing. Correlation ≠ causation. No HIGH supports.\n\nKaufmann dissent: NO","x":1680,"y":-760,"width":380,"height":550,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"asherah-goddess","type":"text","text":"## Asherah: Goddess or Symbol?\n\n**Bidirectional HIGH contradiction · NOT settled**\nThe graph's central unresolved question.\n\n**Evidence:** epigraphy (Kuntillet Ajrud + Khirbet\nel-Qom), archaeology (3000+ JPFs), Ugaritic\nprecedent (Athirat as El's consort), biblical polemics\n\n**Goddess:** Dever · Romer · Day · Cross\n**Symbol:** Smith (14 supports) · Keel & Uehlinger\n\n**Challenge:** -h suffix on 'šrth is grammatically\nambiguous. Iron IIB iconographic gap. Different\nepistemological standards: textual caution vs.\narchaeological parsimony. Unresolvable currently.\n\nKaufmann dissent: NO\n\n[[notes/synthesis/phase4-unknowns-and-convergence]]","x":400,"y":-210,"width":400,"height":520,"color":"3"}
	],
